From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:02:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: support indirect requests

Accept BLKIF_OP_INDIRECT requests when the blkif was connected with a
maximum number of indirect segments (feature-max-indirect-segments, up to
TD_MAX_INDIRECT_SEGMENTS), so that a guest can send requests larger than the
11 segments (44 KiB) of a direct request.

Each request gets its operation and segments in one place (op, nr_segs,
segs): those of the ring descriptor for a direct request, and for an
indirect request its data operation and the segments grant-copied from its
indirect pages, PAGE_SIZE / sizeof(struct blkif_request_segment) per page.
The id and the sector of both kinds of requests are at the same place. The
data buffer of the requests is sized for the largest request of the blkif,
and the per-request arrays for TD_MAX_INDIRECT_SEGMENTS.

The response of an indirect request carries its data operation, as blkback
does. Since nr_segments isn't a field of an indirect request, whether the
request has data, and must be queued, and has a buffer to release, no longer
depends on it.

Based on the indirect-desc branch of Anthoine Bourgeois, for the
multi-queue rings.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
